    {
      "source_id": "sample_000005",
      "question": "During the winter, a clothing store gives a 30% discount for all items. On Tuesdays, it gives an additional $5 off on all sweaters after the winter discount is applied. Without the sales tax, a sweater costs $18.00 after discount. Can we know the original price of the sweater before the discounts?",
      "gold_answer": "32.86",
      "task_type": "math",
      "prompt_group_key": "9aeaa7bfe9761a05439be23bff8736859a073cb3d32468aed6a2e920801175da",
      "direct_prompt_key": "1d80d560ece3a7771e47100ce39cb516c5e2ceeefcfd518b4a3806ece9a22d24",
      "direct_output": "We are given:\n\n- A **30% discount** is applied to all items during winter.\n- On **Tuesdays**, an **additional $5 off** is applied to **all sweaters** after the winter discount.\n- The **original price** of a sweater is **$18.00** after the discount.\n- We are to **determine the original price** of the sweater before the discounts.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Apply the 30% discount\n\nLet the **original price** of the sweater be $ P $.\n\nAfter a 30% discount, the price becomes:\n\n$$\nP \\times (1 - 0.30) = P \\times 0.70 = 18.00\n$$\n\nSo:\n\n$$\nP = \\frac{18.00}{0.70} = 25.71\n$$\n\nThis is the **original price** of the sweater before the $5 off on Tuesdays.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Check if the $5 off is applied on Tuesdays\n\nWe are told that **after the winter discount**, an additional $5 off is applied to **all sweaters** on **Tuesdays**.\n\nSo, the **final price** of the sweater on Tuesday is:\n\n$$\n25.71 - 5 = 20.71\n$$\n\nThis matches the **final price** of the sweater after the discount and the $5 off.\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{25.71}\n$$",
