      "direct_output": "We are given:\n\n- At 20, Alex is $ \\frac{3}{5} $ the age of Ryan.\n\nLet’s denote:\n\n- Alex's current age = 20  \n- Ryan's current age = $ x $\n\nFrom the information, we know:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5}x = 20\n$$\n\nSolving for $ x $:\n\n$$\nx = 20 \\times \\frac{5}{3} = \\frac{100}{3} \\approx 33.33\n$$\n\nSo, **Ryan is approximately 33.33 years old**.\n\nNow, we want to find their **combined age in 10 years**.\n\n- In 10 years, Alex will be $ 20 + 10 = 30 $\n- In 10 years, Ryan will be $ 33.33 + 10 = 43.33 $\n\nSo, their combined age in 10 years is:\n\n$$\n30 + 43.33 = 73.33\n$$\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{73.33}\n$$",
